  {"id":"ge","upper":"Г","lower":"г","name":"гэ","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ge-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ge-name.mp3"},"example":"го́род","exampleMeaning":"city","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ge-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ge-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"A hard g, as in go. Г can also be soft.","soundIpa":"ɡa","soundAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/female/ge-sound.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/male/ge-sound.mp3"},"practiceSyllable":"га"},
  {"id":"de","upper":"Д","lower":"д","name":"дэ","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/de-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/de-name.mp3"},"example":"дом","exampleMeaning":"house","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/de-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/de-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"A short d sound, with the tongue near the upper teeth. Д can also be soft.","soundIpa":"da","soundAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/female/de-sound.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/male/de-sound.mp3"},"practiceSyllable":"да"},
  {"id":"ye","upper":"Е","lower":"е","name":"е","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ye-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ye-name.mp3"},"example":"еда́","exampleMeaning":"food","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ye-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ye-word.mp3"},"kind":"vowel","note":"Stressed е at the start of a word is y + eh. In еда́ it is unstressed and sounds closer to yi. After most consonants, е makes them soft.","soundIpa":"je","soundAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/female/ye-sound.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/male/ye-sound.mp3"},"practiceSyllable":null},
  {"id":"yo","upper":"Ё","lower":"ё","name":"ё","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/yo-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/yo-name.mp3"},"example":"ёлка","exampleMeaning":"fir tree","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/yo-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/yo-word.mp3"},"kind":"vowel","note":"At the start of a word, ё is y + o. After most consonants it makes them soft. Ё is normally stressed.","soundIpa":"jo","soundAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/female/yo-sound.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/male/yo-sound.mp3"},"practiceSyllable":null},
  {"id":"zhe","upper":"Ж","lower":"ж","name":"же","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/zhe-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/zhe-name.mp3"},"example":"жук","exampleMeaning":"beetle","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/zhe-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/zhe-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"Like the s in pleasure, with the tongue farther back. Ж is normally hard.","soundIpa":"ʐ","soundAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/female/zhe-sound.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/male/zhe-sound.mp3"},"practiceSyllable":null},
  {"id":"ze","upper":"З","lower":"з","name":"зэ","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ze-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ze-name.mp3"},"example":"зонт","exampleMeaning":"umbrella","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/ze-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/ze-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"Like z in zoo. З can be hard or soft; this is the hard sound.","soundIpa":"za","soundAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/female/ze-sound.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/male/ze-sound.mp3"},"practiceSyllable":"за"},
  {"id":"i","upper":"И","lower":"и","name":"и","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/i-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/i-name.mp3"},"example":"и́мя","exampleMeaning":"name","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/i-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/i-word.mp3"},"kind":"vowel","note":"Close to ee in see. И usually makes the preceding consonant soft.","soundIpa":"i","soundAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/female/i-sound.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/male/i-sound.mp3"},"practiceSyllable":null},
  {"id":"short-i","upper":"Й","lower":"й","name":"и кра́ткое","nameAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/short-i-name.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/short-i-name.mp3"},"example":"йо́гурт","exampleMeaning":"yogurt","exampleAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/short-i-word.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/male/short-i-word.mp3"},"kind":"consonant","note":"A brief y glide, as in yes. Й is a consonant, not the vowel и.","soundIpa":"j","soundAudio":{"female":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/female/short-i-sound.mp3","male":"/static/audio/alphabet-v1/sounds/male/short-i-sound.mp3"},"practiceSyllable":null},
